    I thinks it would be very spiffy if sworn enemies like elves and orcs
would really go at one another without provocation (ring o' conflict or
having one side as a pet).  A simple priority deal like monsters dealing with one's pets could be set up.  If not hostile to player, the monster will be sure
to take out like HD monsters of opposite alignment and particular racial ha-
tred, otherwise they'll join up to get the player.  In the Amiga Hacklite this
same sort of deal was done with giant spiders and killer bees, both factions would gladly go after one another if more convinient than hitting you, it worked
great.  This maybe impossible coding but I think it would make things a lot
more interesting and give more meaning to friendly monsters (i.e. folk to make
temporary truces of a sort when dealing with mutual enemies).  Another neat
thing would be to see tamed pets not some damned "neutered" when dealing
with other baddies (and baddies being so neutered when fighting your pet, for
that matter).

